Inteligeo, load test of 2026-11-11/12 (no advisory, no upstream fix): creating a map
no longer generates its thumbnail inside the transaction of the request.

Target: GeoNode 4.3.1 as installed by this image (site-packages/geonode). Applied
with `patch -p1 --fuzz=0` from site-packages (paths are geonode/...).

What happened: MapViewSet.create (maps/api/views.py) is @transaction.atomic, and
perform_create ended with resource_manager.set_thumbnail(...), still inside it. The
first save of a resource takes its id from django-sequences
(get_next_value("ResourceBase") in base/models.py), which locks the row of
sequences_sequence until the transaction ends. So every creation of any resource
waited for the thumbnail of the map being created: a GetMap to GeoServer (3.3 s
measured), which in turn asks GeoNode to check the token and needs a free uWSGI
process. With 60 simultaneous creations in the mirror of production, PostgreSQL
showed 35 to 48 `INSERT INTO sequences_sequence ... ('ResourceBase')` waiting for
160 s, no process was left to answer GeoServer, and the liveness probe restarted
GeoNode.

The change: the thumbnail is registered with transaction.on_commit() and runs when
the transaction of create() commits: in the same request, before the response is
sent, with the lock released. Everything else (the maplayers, register_event,
resource_manager.update) stays inside the transaction.

What changes in behaviour:
- The 201 response is built before the thumbnail exists, so its `thumbnail_url` is
  the one the map had when saved; the generated one appears on the next read. (Not
  checked whether 4.3.1 returned the generated URL in this response.)
- A thumbnail that fails leaves the map created without one, as before:
  ResourceManager.set_thumbnail (resource/manager.py) already catches and logs
  every exception.
- perform_create called outside a transaction runs the thumbnail at once
  (on_commit's rule), which is the old behaviour.

Not changed: the update of a map, and the other creations that take the id inside a
transaction with slow work in it (ResourceManager.ingest and copy in
resource/manager.py); those are handled by Inteligeo-load-5-resource-id-lock.patch.

Files touched: geonode/maps/api/views.py, not among the files inteligeo-geonode
copies over the installed package.

Test run (2026-11-12): applied with `patch -p1 --fuzz=0 --no-backup-if-mismatch` on a
copy of site-packages/geonode taken from the 5.5.4 image (which already carries the
earlier patches of this folder), in the order the Dockerfile applies them: 1 file, 1 hunk, 0 FAILED,
0 fuzz; `python -m py_compile` clean. Not run in a pod: the 60 simultaneous creations have to be repeated in the mirror.

